message: "If you cite this computational research thesis, please use the metadata below. No DOI is minted here; do not invent one."
type: thesis
title: "Chain-recurrent labels recoverable from multi-channel ranks that survive stiff–sloppy reduction"
authors:
  - family-names: Ogbonna
    given-names: Kelechi Emeka
    email: kelechiogbonna300@gmail.com
    alias: cloudynirvana
abstract: >-
  Which chain-recurrent versus hybrid-occult labels remain recoverable when
  observation is restricted to the multi-channel Fisher ranks that Thesis #24
  proved survive a stiff–sloppy reduction? On a joint hybrid–smooth toy with
  an unstable focus, a periodic orbit of period 19.874, and two occult guards,
  every trial hits a guard, so the occult class is a two-way split. A linear
  reader sits at chance on the cycle label under both the full channel feature
  and its projection onto the surviving ranks (hold-out accuracies 0.404 and
  0.392 against chance 0.5). The occult-guard label remains recoverable from
  those surviving ranks (hold-out accuracy 1.000). Three practical Fisher
  directions survive the documented reduction. The orbital check is a
  collocation defect, not a certified Conley set. Not a medical device. No
  document DOI.
keywords:
  - chain recurrence
  - hybrid occult modes
  - multi-channel Fisher rank
  - stiff-sloppy reduction
  - label recovery
  - surviving ranks
  - research-only
